{
  "id": "scn_waves",
  "kind": "scene",
  "type": "level",
  "name": "Waves run",
  "notes": "The waves mode's run (the menu's WAVES pad; the classic run is scn_run). A 2 x 2-screen arena in one of the 9 worlds, drawn at random by the picker as in the classic run ('world'): the world's own ground tiles, laid out for the arena (clearings, patches and pictures spread over it, no roads), lit in the middle of the dark; its edge darkens smoothly into black. The player can't step into the dark; the monsters come out of it. A monster whose type is the world's is at home: +10% power and speed and -10% recharge for wild ones, half that (+5% power and speed, -5% recharge) for the player's monster. No floor items lie on the ground when it starts: each level gained opens a menu of 3 cards to choose from, and a fainting monster has a 25% chance to drop one of the classic run's 5 items (at most 3 of each per run, see enm_wave_1). A run started after a win also has the 3 items that win gave (their boosts for the whole run, their words over the player at the start). The wave director brings 10 waves, growing from 3 monsters to 24 plus the boss (see prop_waves); clear them all to win, about 10 minutes. Music: the waves theme (mus_waves) until the boss comes, then the boss theme. Seed: one seed lies on the lit floor each run, at a random one of its 18 spots (away from the player's start); only the player picks it up. It is planted in the menu's garden only if the run is finished, won or lost (see run_seed); quitting or restarting the run loses it. No seed lies on the map while all 4 garden plots are in use, or once the 10 garden items (5 HP UP + 5 POWER UP) are picked up or growing. Garden items: each HP UP picked up adds 5 to the starting HP (and max HP), each POWER UP 2% or 1% to the moves' power (2, 1, 2, 1, 2: +8% for all 5), added silently when the scene starts, so a RESTART gets them again, just the same. World sign: right after the fade-in, the world's name (GREEN MEADOW, EMBER CRATER, CORAL LAGOON, STORM PLATEAU, VERDANT JUNGLE, MIASMA SWAMP, SKY ISLE, HAUNTED HOLLOW or BOULDER CANYON) shows for 3 s in the middle near the top of the screen, like a location sign (the 'sign' variable, drawn by the HUD); the words over the player at the start come after it.",
